 "c": [
  {"i":3301,"t":["measures","time"],"n":"計る is the measuring verb, and 時間を計る (timing) is its typical use; 'actions' is too vague."},
  {"i":3311,"t":["food","routine"],"n":"A meal word. 朝食/昼食/夕食 are also taught as meals of the day in the daily-routine unit; 'time' is loose."},
  {"i":3317,"t":["qualities","position"],"n":"まともに is mostly used for 'properly, decently' (まともに答えない). The head-on sense (まともにぶつかる) is secondary."},
  {"i":3352,"t":["business","work"],"s":{"2":["culture"],"4":["measures"]},"n":"Company and firm. The shrine sense goes to culture. 〜社 as a counter goes to measures; business is already covered in t."},
  {"i":3375,"t":["movement"],"n":"Taught with 迎えに行く/来る (going to meet or pick someone up). The 'death' sense is rare. Family and relationships are only context links."},
  {"i":3400,"t":["movement","weather"],"n":"Being blown away is primarily movement, and the vanish sense isn't weather. Wind is a real but secondary link."}
 ],
 "d": [
  {"i":3308,"keep":[2],"n":"兄ちゃん for calling an unknown young man is common colloquial usage and fits a people unit"},
  {"i":3312,"keep":[4],"n":"茶 as brown (茶髪, 茶色) is common and is taught with colours"},
  {"i":3330,"keep":[],"n":"Alternating current is a technical sense, rare at this level"},
  {"i":3340,"keep":[],"n":"The route sense (typhoon path, etc.) is marginal; the word is taught as one's future course"},
  {"i":3346,"keep":[2],"n":"お腹が空く is a core everyday expression for hunger"},
  {"i":3352,"keep":[4],"n":"Counter 〜社 is common; shrine sense of しゃ appears only in compounds like 神社, taught separately"},
  {"i":3353,"keep":[2],"n":"コーナー as a TV or radio segment is very common in Japanese"},
  {"i":3365,"keep":[3],"n":"〜品 as a counter for dishes or items (一品, 三品) is common at restaurants"},
  {"i":3382,"keep":[],"n":"Getting cured is normally written 治る; this sense of 直る is not taught for health"},
  {"i":3390,"keep":[2],"n":"牛 for beef (牛丼, 牛タン, menus) is very common"},
  {"i":3395,"keep":[],"n":"Majority is still a quantity and already fits numbers"},
  {"i":3396,"keep":[],"n":"A mountain summit is taught as 山頂; 頂点 is mainly abstract or geometric"},
  {"i":3407,"keep":[],"n":"書 as a letter is literary or archaic"},
  {"i":3415,"keep":[2],"n":"〜戦 for matches (決勝戦, 第一戦) is very common in sports"},
  {"i":3422,"keep":[],"n":"Bill passage is news-level vocabulary; passing exams is 合格; the core sense is passing through"},
  {"i":3424,"keep":[],"n":"Japanese uses 演奏 and 劇 for these senses; プレイ in these meanings is rare"},
  {"i":3428,"keep":[4,5],"n":"プラスになる (advantage) and プラス as profit or surplus are common everyday senses"},
  {"i":3432,"keep":[2],"n":"姉ちゃん for addressing a young woman is common colloquial usage and fits people"},
  {"i":3433,"keep":[],"n":"Clue and most-important senses are figurative, used mostly in compounds like キーパーソン"}
 ]
